    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zj-ss-6-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(6) Subject to this section, taking identification material (other than hand prints, finger prints, foot prints or toe prints) from a suspect who:  (a) is at least 10 but under 18, or is incapable of managing his or his affairs; and  (b) has not been arrested and charged; unless a magistrate orders that the material be taken.",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@type": "xsd:decimal",
        "@value": "1.0000"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Identifies temporal overlap between taking identification material and suspect's age or incapability.",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:premiseText": "(6) Subject to this section, a constable must not take identification material (other than hand prints, finger prints, foot prints or toe prints) from a suspect who:  (a) is at least 10 but under 18, or is incapable of managing his or his affairs; and  (b) has not been arrested and charged; unless a magistrate orders that the material be taken."
    },
    {
